---

<section id="rich-blog-post" class="section blog-post" data-layout="standard">
  <!-- kit: rich-blog-post -->
  <article class="container">
    <header class="post-head">
      <ul class="topics" role="list">
        <li><span class="badge">Featured</span></li>
        <li><a href="/journal/topics/recipes">Recipes</a></li>
        <li><a href="/journal/topics/camp">Camp cooking</a></li>
        <li><a href="/journal/topics/cast-iron">Cast iron</a></li>
      </ul>
      <h1>The 30-minute campfire loaf</h1>
      <p class="dek">No starter, no oven, no proofing basket. A Dutch oven, a bag of coals and a dough you mix at lunch.</p>
      <div class="byline">
        <img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/priya-nair/160/160" alt="Portrait of Priya Nair" width="160" height="160" />
        <div>
          <a class="author" href="/authors/priya-nair">Priya Nair</a>
          <p>
            <time datetime="2026-09-24T09:00:00-07:00">24 September 2026</time>
            · Updated <time datetime="2026-09-30T16:20:00-07:00">30 September 2026</time>
            · 7 min read
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <figure class="cover">
      <img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/campfire-loaf/1600/1000" alt="A crusty round loaf on a parchment sling beside a smoking Dutch oven" width="3200" height="2000" />
      <figcaption>Loaf number three of the trip, Deschutes National Forest.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="post-layout">
      <nav class="contents" aria-label="Contents">
        <p class="contents-title">Contents</p>
        <ol>
          <li><a href="#what-you-need">What you need</a></li>
          <li>
            <a href="#mix-at-lunch-bake-at-dusk">Mix at lunch, bake at dusk</a>
            <ol><li><a href="#shaping-without-a-counter">Shaping without a counter</a></li></ol>
          </li>
          <li><a href="#bake">Bake</a></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>Bread is the thing people assume you can't make outside. You can, and it's easier over coals than in most home ovens: a cast-iron Dutch oven is a steam oven with a lid.</p>

        <aside class="takeaways" aria-label="Key takeaways">
          <p class="block-title">Key takeaways</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Mix at lunch, bake at dusk: four hours does the proofing for you.</li>
            <li>Two-thirds of the coals go on the lid.</li>
            <li>Lift the lid once, at 20 minutes.</li>
          </ul>
        </aside>

        <h2 id="what-you-need">What you need</h2>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <caption>Gear for one 900 g loaf</caption>
            <thead>
              <tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">Why</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>5.5 qt Dutch oven</td><td>Holds steam for the first 15 minutes</td></tr>
              <tr><td>18 charcoal briquettes</td><td>About 220°C with 12 on the lid, 6 under</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Parchment sling</td><td>Lowers the dough in without burnt knuckles</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <div class="callout callout--tip">
          <p class="block-title">Count your coals</p>
          <p>Two-thirds on the lid, one-third underneath. Bread burns from the bottom first.</p>
        </div>

        <h2 id="mix-at-lunch-bake-at-dusk">Mix at lunch, bake at dusk</h2>
        <p>Stir 500 g flour, 360 g warm water, 10 g salt and 4 g instant yeast until shaggy. Cover it and forget it for four hours.</p>

        <figure class="wide-figure">
          <img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/campfire-loaf-dough/1600/1000" alt="A shaggy dough in a steel bowl on a camp table" width="1600" height="1000" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Four hours later: doubled and bubbly. Photo: Daniel Okafor</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <h3 id="shaping-without-a-counter">Shaping without a counter</h3>
        <p>Flour the parchment, tip the dough out and fold the four edges into the middle. Flip it seam-down and let it sit while the coals catch.</p>

        <div class="video">
          <iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/Kc7sqbW3f8Y" title="Shaping a campfire loaf (YouTube video)" loading="lazy" allow="accelerometer; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
        </div>

        <figure class="pullquote">
          <blockquote>
            <p>Thin coals, patient lid. Lift it once at 20 minutes and never again.</p>
          </blockquote>
          <figcaption><span class="pq-name">Priya Nair</span>, <span>Caldera product engineering</span></figcaption>
        </figure>

        <div class="inline-cta" data-component="article-cta">
          <p>Baking this weekend? The Ember Dutch Oven ships in two days.</p>
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/products/ember-dutch-oven">Shop the Dutch oven</a>
        </div>

        <h2 id="bake">Bake</h2>
        <p>Lid on for 20 minutes, lid off for 10. Knock the base: hollow means done. A probe should read 96°C.<sup id="fnref-1"><a href="#fn-1" aria-label="Footnote 1">1</a></sup></p>

        <pre><code>Lid on   20 min  ~220°C  12 coals top, 6 under
Lid off  10 min  ~200°C  6 coals under only</code></pre>

        <div class="callout callout--warning">
          <p class="block-title">Never on a picnic table</p>
          <p>A loaded Dutch oven over coals scorches wood. Use the Cable Fold grate or bare ground.</p>
        </div>

        <details class="toggle">
          <summary>Can I use whole wheat?</summary>
          <div class="toggle-body"><p>Swap up to 150 g. Add 20 g more water, the bran drinks it.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="toggle">
          <summary>What if it rains?</summary>
          <div class="toggle-body"><p>The lid keeps rain off the dough. Keep the coals under a tarp until you need them.</p></div>
        </details>

        <a class="product-card" href="/products/ember-dutch-oven" data-component="product-card">
          <img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/caldera-ember-dutch-oven/400/400" alt="Ember Dutch Oven 5.5qt" width="400" height="400" loading="lazy" />
          <span class="pc-body">
            <span class="badge">Used here</span>
            <strong>Ember Dutch Oven 5.5qt</strong>
            <span class="pc-price">$189</span>
          </span>
        </a>

        <ol class="footnotes" aria-label="Footnotes">
          <li id="fn-1">At the centre of the loaf, with an instant-read probe pushed in from the side. <a href="#fnref-1" aria-label="Back to reference 1">↩</a></li>
        </ol>

        <div class="btn-row closing">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/products/ember-dutch-oven">Shop the Dutch oven <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</section>

